<title>UK: European cotton markets quiet, lacking direction.</title>
<headline>European cotton markets quiet, lacking direction.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>West European cotton markets were reported quiet and lacking direction, industry sources said.</p>
<p>Traders are waiting for fresh news in order to be able to gauge future price moves before joining the market, they said.</p>
<p>There were some sales of Central Asian types reported but trade is not expected to revive until the quality and size of crops from some of the major production centres is confirmed.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
